7. **Blood pressure reduction**: The blood pressure reduction in the nose is a result of the activation of the NCN-1 receptor, which in turn leads to the upregulation of the NCN-1 protein. This upregulation of the NCN-1 protein leads to a rise in the blood pressure in the nose.

