To determine the time it takes to deliver the loading dose, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the boy's mass to kilograms (kg)**:
   \[
   1 lb = 0.452 kg \implies 32 \text{ lb} = 32 \times 0.452 = 14.3 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the loading dose**:
   \[
   \text{Loading dose} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.3 \text{ kg} = 286 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time to administer the dose**:
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Loading density}}{\text{Feeding rate}} = \frac{286 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 572 \text{ min}
   \]

