   \[ \text{Na}_2\text{SO}_2\text{O}_2 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Na}_2\text{SO}_2\text{O}_2 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \]
3. The formula `[Pr(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into:  
   \[ [\text{Pt}(\text{NH}_3\text{N}_4\text{Cl}_2] \text{Cl}_2 \rightarrow [\text{Pt}(\text{NH}_3)_4\text{Cl}_2]^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^- \]
4. Thus, the formula `[Pr(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into one ion `[Pr(NH3)4Cl2]^{2+}` and 2 ions `Cl-`.  
5. Thus, the number of chloride ions produced is 2.  

