Lattice Energy = (1/4πε) * (Z1 * Z2 * e^2) / (a)

where 1/4πε is multiplied by the Born-Lange constant (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm).

First, we need to convert the distance from nanometers to meters:

a = 0.231 nm * (1 m / 10^9 nm) = 2.31 x 10^-10 m

Now, we can plug the values into the formula:

L1attice Energy = (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm) * (1 * 1) * (1.602 x 10^-19 C)^2 / (2.31 x 10^-10 m)

Lattice Energy = (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm) * (1) * (2.5632 x 10^-38 m^2) / (2.31 x 10^-10 m)

Lattice Energy = (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm) * (2.5632 x 10^-38 m^2) / (2.31 x 10^-10 m)

