Suppose $f$ is differentiable at $x^*$ and $\nabla f(x^*) \cdot (y - x^*) \geq 0$ for all $y \in \mathcal{U}$. Consider the limit:
\[
\lim_{y \to x^+} \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{|y - x^*|} = \lim_{y \to x^+} \frac{f(x^+) + \nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*) - f(x^*)}{|y - x^*|} = \lim_{y \to x^+} \frac{\nabla f(x^*) (y - x^*)}{|y - x\|}.
\]
