\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \0.01 \times \frac{\text{absorbed dose (mJ)}}{\text{mass (g)}}
\]

Given:
- Absorbed dose = 0.12 J = 120 mJ (since 1 J = 1000 mJ)
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg = 1600 g (since 1 kg = 1000 g)

Substitute the values into the formula:

\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = 0.01 \times \frac{120 \text{ mJ}}{1600 \text{ g}} = 0.01 \times 0.075 \text{ mSv/g} = 0.00075 \text{ mSv}
\]

