- \(n_f\) is the refractive index of the free medium (outside the waveguide),  
- \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective refractive number of the waveguide mode.  

Given:  
- \(k_0 = \frac{2\pi}{1 \times 10^9 \, \text{m}} = 2\pi \times 10^{-9} \, \text{rad/m}\)  
- \(n_f - n_{\text{eff}} = 0.3\)  

Substituting these values:  
\[
L = \frac{1}{2\pi \times 10^{-9} \times 0.3} = \frac{1}{6\pi \times 10^{-9}} \approx 5.3 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{m} = 5 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{m} = 5 \, \mu\text{m}.
\]  

