","The aluminum alloy with 4% copper will have a higher yield strength and lower percent elongation compared to pure aluminum. The strength improvement is due to the presence of the hard intermetallic CuAl$_2$ particles, which act as obstacles to dislocation motion. The lower elongation is due to the increased hardness and reduced ductility caused by these particles and the increased strain hardening.  

The difference in mechanical properties can be explained by the following points:  
