","To compute the curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) in a Cartesian coordinate system, we use the formula:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \begin{vmatrix}
\hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\
\frac{\partial}{\partial x} & \frac{\partial}{\partial y} & \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \\
u & v & w
\end{vmatrix}.
\]
Here, \(\mathbf{V} = \langle u, v, w \rangle\), so \(u = u(x, y)\), \(v = v(x, y)\), and \(w = w(x, y)\). Substituting these into the formula, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \hat{i} \left( \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial v}{\partial y} \right) - \hat{j} \left( \frac{\partial w}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial w}{\partial x} \right) + \hat{k} \left( \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} \right).
\]
Simplifying, we obtain:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \hat{i} \left( \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial v}{\partial y} \right) - \hat{j} \0 + \hat{k} \left( \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} \right).
\]
Thus, the curl of \(\mathbf{V}\) is:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial v}{\partial y} \right) \hat{i} + 0 \hat{j} + \left( \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} \right) \hat{k}.
\]
Thus, the components of the curl are:
\[
\mathbf{V}_x = \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial v}{\partial y}, \quad \mathbf{V}_y = 0, \quad \mathbf{V}_z = \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u}{\partial x}.
\]
Thus, the curl of \(\mathbf{V}\) is:
\[
\boxed{\mathbf{V}_x \hat{i} + \mathbf{V}_z \hat{k}} = \left( \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial v}{\partial y} \right) \hat{i} + \left( \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} \right) \hat{k}.
\]",relevance,"# Task Description
