\]

where:
- \(q\) is the electron charge (\(1.6 \times 10^{-19} \text{ C})\)
- \(\phi_i\) is the built-in potential
- \(\phi_i = \frac{kT}{q} \ln \left( \frac{N_d}{N_a} \right)\)
- \(\epsilon_s\) is the semiconductor permittivity
- \(\epsilon_w\) is the well permittivity
- \(N_d\) is the depletion doping concentration
- \(W_w\) is the width of the oxide region (same as oxide thickness \(W_w = t)\).

The shift in threshold voltage (\(\Delta V_T\)) due to the bias voltage \(V_{BS}\) is given by:

\[
\Delta V_T = \frac{q N_d \phi_i}{2 \varepsilon_s} \left( 1 - \exp\left( -\frac{q V_{BS}}{2 \phi_i} \right) \right)
\]

Given:
