- \(N_d = 10^{16} \text{ cm}^{-3}\)
- \(t = 500 \text{ Å} = 500 \times 10^{-10} \text{ cm}\)

First, calculate \(\phi_i\). For a typical silicon material, \(\phi_i \approx 0.025 \text{ V}\).

Next, calculate \(\epsilon_s\). For silicon, \(\epsilon_s \approx 1.1 \times 10^{-14} \text{ F/cm}\).

Rearranging the shift equation to solve for \(V_{BS}\):

\[
