","The intensity of thermal radiation of a black body in terms of the temperature \( T \) and wavelength \( \lambda \) is given by the Planck displacement law:  
\[
I(\lambda) = \frac{h c}{8\pi \epsilon_0} \frac{1}{\lambda^4} e^{-\frac{hc}{\lambda kT}}
\]  
where:  
- \( I(\lambda) \) is the intensity of thermal radiation at wavelength \( \lambda \)  
- \( h \) is Planck's constant, \( h = 6.626 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J s} \)  
