2. **Force due to the pressure in cylinder B (F_B):**  
   \( F_B = P_B \times A_B = P_B \times \pi \left(\frac{0.025 \text{ m}}{2}\right)^2 = P_B \times \pi \times 0.00625 \text{ m}^2 \)

3. **Force due to the piston's weight (F_w):**  
   \( F_w = m \times g = 25 \text{ kg} \times 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 = 245.175 \text{ N} \)

4. **Force due to atmospheric pressure (F_atm):**  
   \( F_atm = P_{atm} \times A_B = 100 \text{ kPa} \times \pi \left(\frac{0.025 \text{ m}}{2}\right)^2 = 100 \times 10^3 \text{ Pa} \times \pi \times 0.00625 \text{ m}^2 = 1937 \text{ N} \)

The net force on the piston must be zero for equilibrium:  
\[ F_A - F_B - F_w = 0 \]  
\[ F_A = F_B + F_w \]  
\[ F_B = F_A - F_w \]  
\[ P_B \times A_B = 6250 \text{ N} - 245.175 \text{ N} = 3004.825 \text{ N} \]  
\[ P_B = \frac{3004.825 \text{ N}}{1.937 \text{ m}^2} = 1550 \text{ Pa} \]  
But the external pressure is also acting on the bottom of the piston, so the correct equation is:  
\[ F_A = F_w + F_B + F_{atm} \]  
\[ 6250 = 245.175 + 1.937 \times P_B \]  
\[ 6250 - 245.175 = 1.937 \times P_B \]  
\[ 6004.825 = 1.937 \times P_B \]  
\[ P_B = \frac{6004.825}{1.937} = 3190 \text{ Pa} \]  

Thus, the gas pressure in cylinder B is \(\boxed{3190 \text{ Pa}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
