\[
\pi_S = \frac{1}{T} \cdot \text{Power Dissipation} = \frac{1}{T} \cdot \text{Power due to Friction}
\]
The power dissipated by friction is the product of the friction force and the velocity:
\[
\text{Power} = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{1}{T} F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
The entropy production rate is \(\boxed{\dfrac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

