What is the decay length of the evanescent wave in a GaAs core and Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al\(_{0.8}\)As cladding, where \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3\), for a wavelength of 1 μm?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The decay length (\(L\)) of an evanescent wave is given by:  
\[
L = \frac{\1}{k_0 (n_f - n_{\text{eff}})}.
\]  
where:  
- \(k_0 = \frac{2\pi}{c} = \frac{2\pi}{3 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}}\) is the free-space wavelength,  
- \(n_f\) is the refractive index of the free medium (outside the waveguide),  
- \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective refractive number of the waveguide mode.  

Given:  
- \(k_0 = \frac{2\pi}{1 \times 10^9 \, \text{m}} = 2\pi \times 10^{-9} \, \text{rad/m}\)  
- \(n_f - n_{\text{eff}} = 0.3\)  

Substituting these values:  
\[
L = \frac{1}{2\pi \times 10^{-9} \times 0.3} = \frac{1}{6\pi \times 10^{-9}} \approx 5.3 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{m} = 5 \times 10^{-10} \, \text{m} = 5 \, \mu\text{m}.
\]  

Thus, the decay length is \(\boxed{5 \, \mu\text{m}}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
