<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
1. **Calculate the initial closed-loop gain \( A_{vf} \):**
   \[
   A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 + m_v} = \frac{100}{1 + 0.1} = \frac{100}{1.1} \approx 90.9 \text{ dB}
   \]

2. **Calculate the new voltage gain \( A_v' \):**
   The gain decreases by 6 dB, so:
   \[
   A_{vf} = 10^{-0.6} \times 100 = 10^{0.6} \approx 100 \times 0.25 = 25 \text{ dB}
   \]

3. **Calculate the new closed-loop gain \( A_{vf'} \):**
   \[
   A_{vf'} = \frac{A_{vf}'}{1 + m_v} = \frac{25}{1 + 0.1} = \frac{25}{1.1} \approx 22.9 \text{ dB}
   \]

4. **Calculate the percentage change in the closed-loop gain:**
   \[
   \text{Percentage Change} = \left( \frac{A_{vf'} - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{22.9 - 90.9}{90.9} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{-68.0}{90.9} \right) \times 100 \approx -75.1\%
   \]

