2. **Force due to the pressure in cylinder B (F_B):**  
   \( F_B = P_B \times A_B = P_B \times \pi \left(\frac{0.025 \text{ m}}{2}\right)^2 = P_B \times \pi \times 0.00625 \text{ m}^2 \)

3. **Force due to the piston's weight (F_w):**  
   \( F_w = m \times g = 25 \text{ kg} \times 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 = 245.175 \text{ N} \)

4. **Force due to atmospheric pressure (F_atm):**  
   \( F_atm = P_{atm} \times A_B = 100 \text{ kPa} \times \pi \left(\frac{0.025 \text{ m}}{2}\right)^2 = 100 \times 10^3 \text{ Pa} \times \pi \times 0.00625 \text{ m}^2 = 1937 \text{ N} \)

