Now, we need to find the time experienced by the clock in the cabin, which is also moving at the same speed (0.6c) relative to Earth. Since both clock in the cockpit and the clock in the ground are on the same clock, they will experience the same time dilation effect. Therefore, the time experienced by the clock in the cabin will also be 3 years.

So, the time spent by the clock in the cabin is 3 years.
